Z||000001||Cozmo||04-24-2001||01:28 PM||||I've wondered about this too...<BR>Look in the summit racing catalog or go online  <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.summitracing.com/</A> <BR>The BMM-80885 looks like it could be used with a little "finessing"... there are a lot of other types listed that may work also.  A visit to your local speed shop may yield some other info as well as let you examine the shifter first hand.<BR>Keep the forum posted on what you find!<P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 silver 2M6 4spd. Targa <B>"Silver Streak"</B><BR>'86 black auto GT <B>"Blackbird"</B><BR>'87 white auto Coupe <B>"The Duke"</B>||||reg||14
Z||000002||rogergarrison||04-24-2001||01:34 PM||||I had a B&M in an old hot rod I had, far as I know its the best one still. Mine worked great.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-24-2001||07:34 PM||||Take off the shifter suround and look at how the OE one is mounted. I doubt you'll find one that fits in there without a heck of allot of work.||||reg||1
